WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.920
The One PIece Manga just introduced something to&nbsp;
the story, that I would not have expected even&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:04.920 --> 00:00:11.400
in my wildest dreams. Bonney and Luffy have just&nbsp;
discovered an actual light saber inside Vegapunk’s&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:11.400 --> 00:00:17.460
laboratory. So now there is an actual possibility&nbsp;
that we will see a light saber wielding Zoro in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:17.460 --> 00:00:22.440
the story of one Piece. It also might be even more&nbsp;
foreshadowing that Luffy and his crew will go to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:22.440 --> 00:00:28.200
space at some point in the story, based on all the&nbsp;
moon and rocket related technology we have seen in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:28.200 --> 00:00:34.110
One PIece. On top of that, Bonney has turned Luffy&nbsp;
into a 70 year old man, something that Eiichiro&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:34.110 --> 00:00:40.020
Oda had drawn before in an SBS. Not the successful&nbsp;
pirate king version, that looks like Garp,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:40.020 --> 00:00:45.360
but Luffy if he doesn’t achieve his dream. Kuma&nbsp;
might be the second known character next to King&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:45.360 --> 00:00:51.540
who is part of the Lunarian race and while Zoro&nbsp;
is mistrusting Vegapunk Nr. 2, Vegapunk Nr. 1&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:51.540 --> 00:00:57.360
is in contact with the revolutionaries, talking&nbsp;
about his death. Meanwhile, Aokiji is confirmed&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:57.360 --> 00:01:01.860
as an official member of Blackbeard’s crew for&nbsp;
the very first time, looting whole cake island,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:01.860 --> 00:01:07.980
while Law and his men put up a way better fight&nbsp;
against Teach, than any of us could have imagined.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:07.980 --> 00:01:14.520
Does Law have a chance to win this after all? What&nbsp;
is Vegapunk's true goal here? Is Luffy’s new form,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:14.520 --> 00:01:20.100
foreshadowing for a dark future? And most&nbsp;
importantly: Will we see triple wielding&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:20.100 --> 00:01:26.220
darth zoro as an official part of the story? Turns&nbsp;
out, we might already know the answer to all this.

00:01:26.220 --> 00:01:31.800
The current Egghead island arc is the first&nbsp;
part of One PIece’s final saga. And just as Oda&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:31.800 --> 00:01:37.380
promised, it has been setting new standards for&nbsp;
the story already. Currently there are two ongoing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:37.380 --> 00:01:41.700
plot lines running in parallel: The straw hats’&nbsp;
adventure inside the Headquarters of the genius&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:41.700 --> 00:01:47.340
scientist Vegapunk and the epic clash between&nbsp;
Blackbeard and Law. Teach has ambushed Luffy’s&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:47.340 --> 00:01:52.800
brother in arms to get his hands on Kaido’s&nbsp;
poneglyph after his defeat. We have found out that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:52.800 --> 00:01:57.900
Blackbeard didn’t have any of the road poneglyphs&nbsp;
necessary to find the final island laugh tale yet,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:57.900 --> 00:02:03.900
but instead had waited patiently and equipped his&nbsp;
crew with the most powerful devil fruits in order&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:03.900 --> 00:02:09.360
to simply take the information from someone else.&nbsp;
They could do the dirty work for him. As a result,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:09.360 --> 00:02:13.980
a lot is at stake in this fight: Aokiji&nbsp;
and Van Augur have gotten their hands on&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:13.980 --> 00:02:19.620
Big Mom’s road poneglyph as well as Pudding. So&nbsp;
Teach already has 1 stone that Law hasn’t, plus&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:19.620 --> 00:02:24.300
someone who can actually decipher its meaning.&nbsp;
Should Law Lose, Blackbeard will not only have&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:24.300 --> 00:02:31.320
the legendary OP OP no mi in his grasp, but also&nbsp;
get the 2 poneglyphs Law has from Zou and Wano,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:31.320 --> 00:02:37.800
which would have him draw even with Luffy. Plus 3&nbsp;
hostages, Law, Pudding and Kobe to draw out Luffy&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:37.800 --> 00:02:41.160
one he gets his hands on the fourth. I’ll get&nbsp;
to how this fight is going in just a moment.

00:02:41.160 --> 00:02:45.360
Meanwhile, it seems like the straw hats have&nbsp;
had a much better draw with their arrival at&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:45.360 --> 00:02:50.400
egghead island. They most likely aren’t only&nbsp;
about to get a whole lot of sacred knowledge&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:50.400 --> 00:02:55.740
about devil fruits and the history of the world&nbsp;
from Vegapunk, but quite possibly also receive&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:55.740 --> 00:03:02.100
some decisive power upgrades on top. After all,&nbsp;
the island and its technology are 500 year ahead&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:02.100 --> 00:03:06.300
of the rest of the world, which Oda has shown us&nbsp;
in the form of countless advanced technologies,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:06.300 --> 00:03:14.400
including the light saber. A weapon that clearly&nbsp;
is inspired by star wars. And we all know how&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:14.400 --> 00:03:20.340
deadly and powerful a weapon this is in that&nbsp;
universe. So the big question is: Is this simply&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:20.340 --> 00:03:25.620
a funny little easter egg Oda has thrown into&nbsp;
the story, or does this futuristic weapon serve&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:25.620 --> 00:03:30.660
a much more important role for the plot here?&nbsp;
After all we do have a powerful swordsmaster&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:30.660 --> 00:03:36.840
who wants to cut anything. Or could this serve an&nbsp;
even bigger purpose? Let’s look at the evidence.

00:03:36.840 --> 00:03:43.500
The lightsaber in itself already begs to be&nbsp;
used in my opinion just looking at it and seeing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:43.500 --> 00:03:48.120
Luffy’s reaction to it. It definitely wouldn’t be&nbsp;
the first futuristic weapon related to Vegapunk&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:48.120 --> 00:03:53.520
in the straw hat crew. After all, as you can see&nbsp;
in these panels, we have Franky’s cyborg powers,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:53.520 --> 00:03:58.860
Nami’s climat tact and Sanji’s genetic&nbsp;
modifications. Would Eiichiro Oda ever&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:58.860 --> 00:04:04.260
turn Zoro into the One Piece version of a&nbsp;
Jedi or Sith? Well, we don’t have to wonder,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:04.260 --> 00:04:11.520
because he has already done that. Twice: This&nbsp;
is official artwork Oda did in 1999 for the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:11.520 --> 00:04:17.940
release of The Phantom Manice with Zoro as anakin&nbsp;
skywalker. And then, in 2015 for the release of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:17.940 --> 00:04:25.500
the force awakens, he drew the straw hats as star&nbsp;
wars figures. Again Zoro as a Jedi slash sith. And&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:25.500 --> 00:04:30.000
of course we have all the other space related&nbsp;
technology in One PIece. We have seen a ton of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:30.000 --> 00:04:35.340
rocket shaped objects in the lab. There are ships&nbsp;
capable of space travel, like Enel’s arch maxime&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:35.340 --> 00:04:39.960
and of course we already know from Enel’s cover&nbsp;
story that there used to be a whole civilization&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:39.960 --> 00:04:46.500
on one of the one piece moons with advanced&nbsp;
technology. And of of course: Space pirates.&nbsp;

00:04:46.500 --> 00:04:51.600
Now does all this prove that Zoro will start&nbsp;
yielding a lightsaber for the rest of the series?&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:51.600 --> 00:04:58.020
well, yeah it could. Eiichiro Oda has been a&nbsp;
big Sci Fi and star wars fan and taken a lot&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:58.020 --> 00:05:04.080
of inspiration from it for his own story. When you&nbsp;
look at the reflection of this TV in Oda’s office,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:04.080 --> 00:05:09.120
you can see a live size model of R2D2&nbsp;
parked under a shelf. He also has a life&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:09.120 --> 00:05:13.560
size terminator by the way, in case you were&nbsp;
curious where the inspiration for franky came&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:13.560 --> 00:05:19.500
from. Of course the lightsaber could also just&nbsp;
end up being a small token of his appreciation&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:19.500 --> 00:05:25.140
for the star wars story or simply a gadget that&nbsp;
Zoro or some other character uses in the story,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:25.680 --> 00:05:32.040
but it could mean much much more than this. As you&nbsp;
know, Oda usually doesn’t just draw attention to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:32.040 --> 00:05:38.280
things for no reason. The connection with Zoro&nbsp;
is quite obvious too: Lightsaber or laser sword&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:38.280 --> 00:05:43.200
and the crew’s swordsman. Oda clearly thought&nbsp;
along the same lines as well, drawing Zoro as&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:43.200 --> 00:05:49.620
a force wielder more than just once and as far&nbsp;
back as 1999. It’s obviously something he would&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:49.620 --> 00:05:55.800
like to draw in his story. It might just be&nbsp;
the upgrade that Zoro has been waiting for,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:55.800 --> 00:06:01.920
looking for a unique weapon that truly can&nbsp;
cut anything and would allow for completely&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:01.920 --> 00:06:07.740
new techniques and powers from here on out. And&nbsp;
while i find it unlikely that he will trade in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:07.740 --> 00:06:13.800
all of his traditional blades for lightsabers, he&nbsp;
might simply have this as a special fourth weapon&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:13.800 --> 00:06:20.160
from now on. Or he could keep it safe until he&nbsp;
needs it. For example, in case that the straw&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:20.160 --> 00:06:26.210
hats ever went to space. Because as you’ve seen,&nbsp;
there are a lot of things hinting at this. There&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:26.210 --> 00:06:30.780
is actually quite a lot of evidence out there,&nbsp;
that Laugh Tale itself may be located on the moon,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:30.780 --> 00:06:34.500
but that’s a whole different video. Let me know if&nbsp;
you’d like to see that. To stick with the evidence&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:34.500 --> 00:06:40.080
so far, we do know that there are space pirates,&nbsp;
similar to what we have in star wars, there is an&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:40.080 --> 00:06:45.180
ancient and lost city slash temple of an advanced&nbsp;
civilisation on the moon, again similar to star&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:45.180 --> 00:06:49.920
wars and all of its ancient history and lore.&nbsp;
And even if this is stretching it a little bit,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:49.920 --> 00:06:56.280
i know, but you could make the case that Haki&nbsp;
and the force are not all to different either.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:56.280 --> 00:07:00.960
just like the force, you can use Haki to control&nbsp;
living things and increase your fighting ability,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:00.960 --> 00:07:07.140
while its strength is dependent on the users&nbsp;
strength of will and training. I mean Rayleigh is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:07.140 --> 00:07:13.980
as Obi Wan a character as it gets when he teaches&nbsp;
Luffy haki. So should the story one day take us&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:13.980 --> 00:07:21.540
to space, a lightsaber or three would really be&nbsp;
the only appropriate weapon for Zoro. And now&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:21.540 --> 00:07:29.160
we know that it exists. Which i think is a win no&nbsp;
matter what way you look at it. Vegapunk is really&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:29.160 --> 00:07:34.260
adding endless new possibilities to the story&nbsp;
and hopefully the crew will leave with a bunch of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:34.260 --> 00:07:41.580
power upgrades. But what really is Vegapunk up to?&nbsp;
Well, the manga just told us a little bit more.

00:07:42.360 --> 00:07:49.200
We know that Dr. Vegapunk is not just one person,&nbsp;
but an entity consisting of one original body and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:49.200 --> 00:07:55.620
6 clones. And while we don’t quite know yet how&nbsp;
it works, each of these 6 versions of vegapunk&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:55.620 --> 00:08:01.500
can think and act independently with their own&nbsp;
name, personality and agenda. If you want a detail&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:01.500 --> 00:08:06.060
breakdown of each of the 6’s inspirations&nbsp;
and possible research goals, i made a whole&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:06.060 --> 00:08:11.400
video about that you can check out. But for this,&nbsp;
let’s look at the 3 vegapunks we have met so far:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:11.400 --> 00:08:17.640
Vegapunk Nr. 1 Shaka, based on a famous Zulu king.&nbsp;
Vegapunk nr. 2, lilith, based on Adam’s first&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:17.640 --> 00:08:24.720
wife, who was banished from paradise and turned&nbsp;
into the arch demon. And Vegapunk nr.5 Atlas,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:24.720 --> 00:08:30.720
who is based on the titan who was sentenced to&nbsp;
carrying the heavens on his shoulders. Shaka&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:30.720 --> 00:08:36.000
seems to have a lot of authority, as he is able to&nbsp;
command lilith to bring the remaining straw hats&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:36.000 --> 00:08:42.960
to him. He also is in contact to Dragon, finally&nbsp;
confirming the connection between Vegapunk and the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:42.960 --> 00:08:48.480
revolutionaries we all have been speculating&nbsp;
about. Lilith meanwhile seems to be quite&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:48.480 --> 00:08:53.100
agressive and battle hungry. She wanted to get&nbsp;
rid of the straw hats the moment she saw them.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:53.100 --> 00:08:59.340
Zoro has decided to protect the Sunny with Brook,&nbsp;
because he doesn’t trust Lilith. And atlas seems&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:59.340 --> 00:09:05.400
to have a quite simple and kind personality&nbsp;
so far, which seems to clash with her trait&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:05.400 --> 00:09:10.620
of violence. We haven’t seen the remaining&nbsp;
3 vegapunks nor the original one so far.

00:09:10.620 --> 00:09:14.460
Now obviously, we are still very early in this&nbsp;
arc. We don’t really know yet how the entire&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:14.460 --> 00:09:20.400
Vegapunk with 7 bodies thing really works and&nbsp;
what relationship they have with each other.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:20.400 --> 00:09:24.660
But based on the evidence we have gotten so&nbsp;
far, I really like the idea that since each&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:24.660 --> 00:09:30.120
Vegapunk can make their own decisions with their&nbsp;
own personality, each of them could have different&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:30.120 --> 00:09:36.900
agendas too. Shaka for instance, could be the&nbsp;
Vegapunk that has been feeding information to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:36.900 --> 00:09:41.640
the revolutionaries and helping them with Kuma.&nbsp;
Meanwhile, a character like Lilith could be loyal&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:41.640 --> 00:09:47.280
to the world government, while maybe again another&nbsp;
one might become friends with pirates like Luffy.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:47.280 --> 00:09:53.940
The answer to who’s side Vegapunk is on, could&nbsp;
simply be everybody’s and nobody’s. And i find&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:53.940 --> 00:09:59.520
that a very intriguing premise for this entire&nbsp;
arc. That could mean that we have factions of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:59.520 --> 00:10:05.820
Vegapunk fighting amongst each other. It could&nbsp;
be a little bit like the pixar movie inside out,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:05.820 --> 00:10:10.740
where Vegapunk has personified different parts of&nbsp;
himself. I like this idea a lot, because we still&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:10.740 --> 00:10:16.380
don’t really have a clear objective or villain for&nbsp;
this arc. The straw hats have no goal right now.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:16.380 --> 00:10:21.480
No one to meet up with. No one to defeat yet.&nbsp;
Just sightseeing basically. So having Vegapunk&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:21.480 --> 00:10:27.240
be the villain AND the ally in this arc would&nbsp;
be fantastic. Especially with CP0 in the mix.

00:10:27.240 --> 00:10:32.460
On top of that we have the reveal that Kuma is not&nbsp;
only Bonnies father and a former revolutionary,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:32.460 --> 00:10:37.200
but also from a special race,&nbsp;
which given his dark skin most&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:37.200 --> 00:10:40.980
likely means that Kuma is a Lunarian&nbsp;
just like king. This would of course&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:40.980 --> 00:10:47.640
explain why Vegapunk wanted to experiment&nbsp;
on him, like he did with King, who escaped,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:47.640 --> 00:10:53.940
and why the pacifista have now evolved into the&nbsp;
Seraphim, that have strong Lunarian properties.

00:10:53.940 --> 00:10:59.460
At the same time, Luffy has now been turned&nbsp;
into the 70 year old version of himself, that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:59.460 --> 00:11:06.000
Oda drew as the ‘bad timeline’. In this&nbsp;
reality luffy never fulfills his dream&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:06.000 --> 00:11:12.240
to become pirate king and ends up bitter.&nbsp;
Does this mean that Luffy’s future right&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:12.240 --> 00:11:16.320
now means that he will not reach his dream? I&nbsp;
like the idea a lot that at some point Bonney&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:16.320 --> 00:11:22.080
turns Luffy old again and this time he’s&nbsp;
the successful version that looks like garp,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:22.080 --> 00:11:29.160
symbolizing that luffy is on the right path&nbsp;
again. Maybe, it’s because of Luffy’s biggest&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:29.160 --> 00:11:34.620
rival Blackbeard threatening to catch up to&nbsp;
him and taking out one of his biggest allies.

00:11:35.700 --> 00:11:41.700
The fighting sequence between Law and Teach&nbsp;
is really something else. We all kind of knew&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:41.700 --> 00:11:49.320
that Law was strong, but he’s holding his ground&nbsp;
here much better than I anticipated. He clearly&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:49.320 --> 00:11:53.880
has learned a lot from his fight with Kaido and&nbsp;
Big Mom. Law uses his awakened abilities quite&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:53.880 --> 00:11:58.980
comfortably, managing to land some serious&nbsp;
hits on Blackbeard, who counters with both&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:58.980 --> 00:12:04.800
of his devil fruit abilities. I’m especially&nbsp;
surprised to see that Law’s crew is holding&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:04.800 --> 00:12:10.020
themselves against Blackbeard’s crew. I did&nbsp;
not see that coming, especially because Law’s&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:10.020 --> 00:12:15.840
crew was not at all involved in the raid on&nbsp;
Onigashima. Turns out they can actually fight.

00:12:16.500 --> 00:12:20.700
Now I will stick to my opinion that&nbsp;
Law, despite how strong he has gotten,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:22.920 --> 00:12:30.840
has no chance of winning this, simply because&nbsp;
it would make no sense story wise. However, I do&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:30.840 --> 00:12:36.000
believe that he might manage to get away instead&nbsp;
of getting captured. One way or the other I do&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:36.000 --> 00:12:41.760
think that Blackbeard will get his hands on Law’s&nbsp;
two poneglyphs here, really raising the stakes&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:41.760 --> 00:12:47.700
between him and Luffy to as high as possible. If&nbsp;
not now then when will Teach get those 2 stones.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:48.360 --> 00:12:54.840
He has planned all this so carefully that he&nbsp;
really can’t afford to lose here. And in case&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:54.840 --> 00:13:01.320
you’re curious what Blackbeard’s genius plan has&nbsp;
been, you should really check out that video next.

